Dr. Adams,

I originally deleted my post this morning because I discovered I was using the wrong null.model in my pairwise tests. I was mistakenly using the full model given under "reveal.model.design" as my null in the pairwise function.

I am now getting some significant results in my pairwise tests although they still have a small effect size. I'm glad you were still able to respond because cross-validation had not crossed my mind. I will definitely be looking into this and and incorporating it into my analyses. It sounds like it would be especially beneficial to have for reviewers to justify my choice of model with weak effect sizes.

Thank you for your time,

Aaron

